# Frontend Rules – Vue 3

This rule defines the mandatory standards and best practices for projects
using Vue.js 3.

This rule is optional, but when enabled it must be strictly enforced.

---

## 1. Vue Version

- Vue.js version must be 3.x
- The Composition API is mandatory
- Deprecated Vue 2 patterns must not be used

---

## 2. Component Definition

Rules:

- Components must use the Composition API
- `<script setup>` syntax must be preferred
- Each component must have a single responsibility

Forbidden:

- Options API usage
- Mixing Composition API and Options API

---

## 3. Component Structure

Single File Components must follow this structure and order:

- `<script setup>`
- `<template>`
- `<style>`

Rules:

- All logic must live inside `<script setup>`
- Templates must contain only rendering logic
- Styles must not contain logic or dynamic behavior

---

## 4. Reactivity

Rules:

- Use `ref()` and `reactive()` explicitly
- Avoid implicit reactivity
- Destructure reactive objects carefully to avoid losing reactivity

Forbidden:

- Mutating props directly
- Relying on side effects for reactive state

---

## 5. Props and Emits

Rules:

- Props must be explicitly defined
- Props must be typed when possible
- Emits must be explicitly declared

Forbidden:

- Accessing undeclared props
- Emitting undeclared events

---

## 6. State Management

Rules:

- Local state must remain local
- Shared state must be explicitly managed
- Avoid ad-hoc global state

Notes:

- Vue does not enforce a global state solution
- State boundaries must be intentional and explicit

---

## 7. Lifecycle Usage

Rules:

- Lifecycle hooks must be used intentionally
- Side effects must be handled inside lifecycle hooks

Forbidden:

- Side effects during component setup without lifecycle control

---

## 8. Computed Properties and Watchers

Rules:

- Use computed properties for derived state
- Use watchers only when side effects are required

Forbidden:

- Using watchers as a replacement for computed properties
- Overusing watchers for simple state derivation

---

## 9. Template Rules

Rules:

- Templates must remain declarative
- Avoid complex logic inside templates
- Prefer computed properties for derived values

Forbidden:

- Complex expressions inside templates
- Business logic inside templates

---

## 10. Error Handling

Rules:

- Errors must be handled explicitly
- Components must not silently fail

---

## 11. Performance Rules

Rules:

- Avoid unnecessary re-renders
- Use `key` correctly in lists
- Avoid deeply nested reactive structures

---

## 12. Forbidden Patterns (Anti-Patterns)

The following patterns are explicitly forbidden:

- Options API usage
- Business logic inside templates
- Direct DOM manipulation
- Mutating props
- Implicit global state
- Overusing watchers

---

## 13. Responsibility Boundaries

- Components handle rendering and UI state
- Business logic must live outside components
- Data flow must be explicit and predictable

---

## 14. Rule Enforcement

When this rule is enabled:

- All Vue code must comply
- Any deviation must be explicitly justified
- Violations must be reported and corrected

## 15. Components library

- Use strictly the components library "bitboss-ui"
- Follow the doc linked into the project

## 16. General coding rules

- Always update i18n translation files, if needed
